WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.320
[Upbeat music begins and plays during the
video]

00:00:03.512 --> 00:00:07.650
[Dr. Dina Demner-Fushman] When people need
information, what they really like is to ask

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:15.599
a question and get a really good comprehensive
answer, and also know that the answer is true

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:17.270
and correct.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:24.240
When I started my independent clinician career,
I had lots of questions but I was sometimes

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.780
not even sure if I'm getting the right answer.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:34.040
Question answering is this system has to understand
the question, what the question is about,

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.300
and why is it asked.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.569
When the answer is found, it's usually not
a single answer.

00:00:39.569 --> 00:00:42.770
It's parts of the answer in different places.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.670
It's multiple answers.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:50.775
So all of that then needs to be condensed
into one comprehensive answer with evidence

00:00:50.775 --> 00:00:52.890
to where the answer came from.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.920
So that's the focus of my research.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:03.350
On the surface, very similar questions asked
by clinicians, and by the public, should be

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.445
answered very differently.

00:01:05.445 --> 00:01:12.710
Different deep learning systems are needed
to find the answers to the same question asked

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:13.850
by two different people.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:14.850
[Silence]

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.050
[Upbeat music starts again]

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:21.750
The long-term goal is one entry point to all
the NLM resources.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:31.166
It doesn't matter who the person is and how
they ask their question or look for information.

00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:36.340
We should be able to recognize what the person
needs and provide it.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:45.740
There is no one, other than NLM, who is specifically
dedicated to biomedical information retrieval

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:49.740
-- biomedical question answering.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:55.216
Although industry seems that they are doing
that kind of research as well, it is not their

00:01:55.216 --> 00:01:56.263
main focus.

00:01:56.263 --> 00:02:03.867
Whereas, we keep people focused on what really
matters for health and advancing medicine.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:10.671
[Music]

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:20.630
[Music fades to silence]

